{"step_index":188,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T15:00:59Z","thinking":"**Examining Roman Domination Concepts**\n\nThe definitions for `IsRomanDominatingFunction`, `romanWeight`, and `romanDominationNumber` appear. `IsRomanDominatingFunction` checks if a function assigns a value to each vertex such that if a vertex's value is 0, it has an adjacent vertex with value 2. `romanWeight` sums the values assigned to each vertex. The roman domination number then seems to be related to some sort of minimization or optimal function with these constraints.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"grep_search","args":{"MatchPerLine":true,"Query":"theorem ","SearchPath":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/lean_project","toolAction":"Search theorems in LeanProject","toolSummary":"Search theorems in lean_project"}}]}
